<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">16 August in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">8 events that happened on 16 August, from 942 to 1977.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/hamdanid-dynasty" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hamdanid-dynasty.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/942">942 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">1,084 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Hamdanids and Baridis fight for Baghdad at al-Mada'in</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Near al-Mada'in in central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iraq">Iraq</a>, the armies of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hamdanid-dynasty">Hamdanids</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mosul">Mosul</a> and the Baridis of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/basra">Basra</a> began a four-day battle for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baghdad">Baghdad</a>, the Abbasid capital. The Hamdanids prevailed but were too exhausted to pursue, and the Baridis withdrew to Basra.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hamdanid-dynasty">Hamdanid dynasty</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baghdad">Baghdad</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abbasid-caliphate">Abbasid Caliphate</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/963">963 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">1,063 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Nikephoros II Phokas is crowned Byzantine emperor</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The general <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nikephoros-ii-phokas">Nikephoros II Phokas</a> was crowned emperor, swearing to protect the two sons of the late Romanos II, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/basil-ii">Basil II</a> and Constantine VIII, who were already co-emperors. He was murdered by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-i-tzimiskes">John Tzimiskes</a> in 969.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nikephoros-ii-phokas">Nikephoros II Phokas</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byzantine-empire">Byzantine Empire</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1328">1328 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">698 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Gonzaga family takes power in Mantua</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-gonzaga">House of Gonzaga</a> seized power in Mantua, in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lombardy">Lombardy</a>, beginning a rule that lasted until 1708. Under Federico II Gonzaga, its first duke, Mantua later became a duchy, which in 1531 also acquired <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/montferrat">Montferrat</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-gonzaga">House of Gonzaga</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1513">1513 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">513 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Henry VIII's army routs French cavalry at the Battle of the Spurs</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">English and imperial troops put French cavalry to flight near Guinegate, the speed of their retreat giving the battle its name. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/therouanne">Thérouanne</a> surrendered days later.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1780">1780 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">246 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Cornwallis routs the Americans at Camden</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">British forces under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-cornwallis-1st-marquess-cornwallis">Lord Cornwallis</a> shattered Horatio Gates's army at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/camden-south-carolina">Camden, South Carolina</a>. The defeat led to Nathanael Greene taking command in the south.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1819">1819 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">207 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Cavalry attack a reform meeting at Peterloo</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Yeomanry and hussars charged a crowd of some 60,000 at St Peter's Field, Manchester, gathered to demand parliamentary reform. About 18 people died and hundreds were injured.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1896">1896 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">130 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Gold is found on Bonanza Creek in the Klondike</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">George Carmack, Skookum Jim and Dawson Charlie struck gold on a tributary of the Klondike River in the Yukon. When news reached the south in 1897, some 100,000 people set out for the goldfields.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1977">1977 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">49 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Elvis Presley dies at Graceland</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Elvis Presley was found dead at his Memphis home, aged 42. The 'King of Rock and Roll' had sold hundreds of millions of records and transformed popular music.</p></div></li></ol>
